Subject: [PATCH 1/2] PUBLISH-FIX-110: the guard shed the prey - runners are
 shed last now

The owner asked why the snake did not bite ZETA. This is why.

Deployment 2b2047d0. The fitness funnel put ZETA on the stage FIRST -
57.245% range in the hour, fit 10.408x - and six minutes later the
tape's resource guard threw it away:

  04:13:34 HOT LANE: ZETA joins the deep tape now (57.245% 1h
           (fit 10.408x); $0.1M 24h; hot slots 1/20)
  04:19:18 RESOURCE_WARNING heap=737MB lag=3101ms (LAG_SUSTAINED)
           - shedding 7 lowest-volume pairs: ZETA RARI UAI NIL CFG CELR PTB

The guard shed LOWEST 24-HOUR VOLUME first and re-admitted highest
volume first. The coins this application hunts are small - that is what
a small-cap runner IS - so under any pressure it dumped the prey and
kept the thirty majors that never move. Seven runners in one stroke,
every major untouched, the runners due back last. Built to protect the
machine from the point.

Now: shed in order of FITNESS (the fit the hot lane recorded on
adoption, FIX-98), least fit first; a pair with no fit at all - the
static base universe - goes before any pair that has one; ties fall
back to volume as before; re-admission is fittest first. WHEN to shed
is untouched (same heap ceiling, lag threshold, sustain and calm
rules); only WHOM. Exposure is still never shed. Authority NONE.

tape/resource-law.js version 1 -> 2; tape/run.js passes the fit and
re-pinned in test/social-4f-scope.test.js. Fenced by
test/publish-fix-110-runners-shed-last.test.js (5), including the exact
seven-runner shape from 2b2047d0 and that with no fitness anywhere the
old law stands byte for byte.

