From 4ef17bebf4fc8f5cf8cbb1866bf3bca139f9c84c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 04:30:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] PUBLISH-FIX-111: the flow windows were the main thread -
 bounded, exactly

Production 2b2047d0 at 04:19, the sampled minute at 100% busy with
twenty candidates on the stage:

  CPU PROFILE 60s: busy 60026ms idle 178ms . top: cmp 13% . parseDecimal
  8% . (gc) 7% . fromNumberLexeme 6% . canonicalJson 6% . windowFacts 5%
  . parseDecimalUncached 4% . onBook 3%

and in the same minutes, six times on NEAR and SUI - the two most
active crossers - `hypothesis lock not durable within 10 s`, and a
resource shed at lag=3101ms.

Every window query scanned the WHOLE retained trade array - 25 minutes
of prints - to find a 15-second window, twice (queryEpoch, then the
filter), with decimal-string arithmetic per print, up to four times a
second per candidate. The cost rose with the trade rate: the Judge was
slowest on exactly the coins that were running.

The fix is a lower bound and it is EXACT. validTradeClock (enforced at
insertion) guarantees eventTs <= receiptTs, so a print inside the
window by eventTs has receiptTs >= startTs; the tracker's array is in
receipt order; a binary search on receiptTs skips only prints that
could never be in the window. The tracker passes `sortedByReceipt` and
turns it off for good the moment a print arrives out of receipt order.
A plain array without the hint is scanned from the start exactly as
before. No feature value, window law, epoch law, coverage law or
rounding moved. judge-differential (recorded inputs replayed on both
trees) is green.

Fenced by test/publish-fix-111-bounded-windows.test.js (5): bounded ==
full over every window function and all 21 RV60 windows; the tracker's
readings equal hint-less readings incl. a widened window; disorder turns
it off and readings stay correct; an epoch change restores it; >= 4x
faster on a 15 s window over 40,000 prints.

Frozen: judge 9122a83068c6 -> b8d814731a3a, all 39a03bf6645e ->
ad323dca8b88; execution and watch/watch.js unchanged. Recorded as
docs/JUDGE-PAPER-AUDIT.md 4.42 (and FIX-110 as 4.41).

